{% comment %}
  The shops, laid out as a spread rather than a list. Each is a photograph
  with its name under it on the left and an arrow on the right; the arrow
  opens the details — address, hours, whatever the owner puts there — by
  sliding them down under the name.

  Each block points at a `location` metaobject rather than carrying its own
  photo and copy: the shop's own data (address, hours, description, photo)
  lives in one place and is reused wherever a shop needs to be shown, rather
  than being retyped per block the way the coffee page's roaster credit
  points at a `roaster` metaobject for the same reason.

  Two columns, and the shops take them in turn: the first sits left, the
  second right and dropped a little, the third left again. Each column keeps
  its own rhythm because a shop with a longer photograph pushes only its own
  side down. Below 750px it is one column and nothing is offset.

  Editorial rather than a grid of equal tiles: each block picks its own size
  (a width, as a share of its column) and photograph shape, so the spread
  reads as considered rather than uniform. What does not vary is the outer
  edge — a left-column shop's left edge and a right-column shop's right edge
  always sit on the page margin, the same one the header uses, so the sizes
  differ without the page ever looking misaligned. Only the inner edge, and
  the vertical drop, move.

  Every photograph is inside a <parallax-frame>, so it drifts against the
  page as it scrolls by.

  Not a `{% doc %}`: those are not valid in sections.
{% endcomment %}

{% liquid
  assign placeholders = 'hero-apparel-1,detailed-apparel-1,hero-apparel-3,product-apparel-1' | split: ','
  assign drop = section.settings.drop | default: 10
%}

<div class="locations" style="--locations-drop: {{ drop }}vw;" {{ section.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign slot = forloop.index0 | modulo: placeholders.size
      assign placeholder = placeholders[slot]
      assign ratio = block.settings.aspect_ratio | default: '1 / 1'
      assign width = block.settings.width | default: 85

      assign shop = block.settings.location
      assign name = shop.name.value
      assign photo = shop.photo.value
      assign address = shop.address.value
      assign hours = shop.hours.value
      assign has_description = shop.description.value

      assign has_info = false
      if address != blank or hours != blank or has_description != blank
        assign has_info = true
      endif
    -%}
    <article class="location" style="--location-width: {{ width }}%;" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
      <parallax-frame class="location__media" style="aspect-ratio: {{ ratio }};">
        {%- if photo != blank -%}
          {{ photo | image_url: width: 1400 | image_tag: sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 30vw, 100vw', class: 'location__image', loading: 'lazy' }}
        {%- else -%}
          {{ placeholder | placeholder_svg_tag: 'location__image' }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </parallax-frame>

      {%- if has_info -%}
        <details class="location__details">
          <summary class="location__summary">
            <span class="location__name">{{ name }}</span>
            <span class="location__mark" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'logo-arrow' %}</span>
          </summary>
          <div class="location__info">
            {%- if has_description != blank -%}
              <div class="location__description rte">{{ shop.description | metafield_tag }}</div>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if address != blank -%}
              <p class="location__address">{{ address }}</p>
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- if hours != blank -%}
              <div class="location__hours">
                <p class="location__hours-heading">{{ section.settings.hours_label | default: 'Opening hours' }}</p>
                {%- assign hour_lines = hours | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
                {%- for line in hour_lines -%}
                  {%- assign line_text = line | strip -%}
                  {%- if line_text != blank -%}
                    <p>{{ line_text }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        </details>
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="location__summary location__summary--plain">
          <span class="location__name">{{ name }}</span>
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </article>
  {%- endfor -%}
</div>

{% render 'parallax' %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .locations {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding: 0 var(--ocp-page-margin) 8rem;
    background: var(--color-background);
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }

  .location {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .location__media {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .location__media .location__image {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .location__summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-block: 0.6rem;
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    font-family: var(--font-subheading--family);
    font-size: var(--ocp-text-size);
    line-height: var(--ocp-leading-snug);
    letter-spacing: var(--ocp-letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .location__summary--plain {
    cursor: default;
  }

  .location__summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .location__mark {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 0.7em;
    transition: transform 0.3s ease;
  }

  .location__mark svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* Points down-right at rest — there is more here. Open, it turns to point
     up-right: the same gesture reversed. */
  .location__details[open] .location__mark {
    transform: rotate(-90deg);
  }

  /* The details slide down. Only where the browser can animate to an
     intrinsic height; elsewhere they simply appear, which is a fair fallback. */
  .location__details {
    interpolate-size: allow-keywords;
  }

  .location__details::details-content {
    block-size: 0;
    overflow: clip;
    transition:
      block-size 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1),
      content-visibility 0.45s allow-discrete;
  }

  .location__details[open]::details-content {
    block-size: auto;
  }

  .location__info {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 0.25rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-body--family);
    font-size: var(--ocp-text-size);
    line-height: var(--ocp-leading-text);
    letter-spacing: var(--ocp-letter-spacing);
  }

  .location__description > :first-child {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .location__description > :last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }

  .location__address {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .location__hours {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .location__hours p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .location__hours-heading {
    font-family: var(--font-subheading--family);
    letter-spacing: var(--ocp-letter-spacing);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .locations {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 8rem 0;
    }

    /*
     * The outer edge is fixed to the column's own edge — which, since the
     * container's own padding is the page margin, is the same edge the
     * header sits on — and only the inner edge moves with each block's own
     * width. A left-column shop is flush left and varies on the right; a
     * right-column shop is flush right and varies on the left. Every second
     * shop also drops by the section's own setting.
     */
    .location:nth-child(odd) {
      width: var(--location-width, 85%);
      margin-inline-end: auto;
    }

    .location:nth-child(even) {
      width: var(--location-width, 85%);
      margin-inline-start: auto;
      margin-block-start: var(--locations-drop);
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .location__mark,
    .location__details::details-content {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Locations",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "location",
      "name": "Location",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "metaobject",
          "id": "location",
          "metaobject_type": "location",
          "label": "Shop",
          "info": "Name, photo, address, hours and description all live on the shop itself — add or edit one under Content > Metaobjects."
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "aspect_ratio",
          "label": "Photograph shape",
          "options": [
            { "value": "1 / 1", "label": "Square" },
            { "value": "4 / 5", "label": "Portrait" },
            { "value": "3 / 2", "label": "Landscape" }
          ],
          "default": "1 / 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "width",
          "label": "Size",
          "info": "Share of its column. The outer edge (against the page margin) never moves — only the inner edge does, which is what varies the size.",
          "min": 50,
          "max": 100,
          "step": 5,
          "unit": "%",
          "default": 85
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "hours_label",
      "label": "Hours heading",
      "default": "Opening hours"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "drop",
      "label": "How far the right-hand shops sit lower",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "vw",
      "default": 10
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Locations",
      "blocks": [{ "type": "location" }, { "type": "location" }]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
